            <div xml:id="d509">

                <pb facs="0631" n="529" xml:id="pg529"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 406/245–259.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Jay to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-09-07"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 7, 1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 430.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 408 of August 23, I
                    have the honor to transmit herewith carefully revised translations of the
                    ordinances recently promulgated relating to the protection of industrial and
                    literary property in Korea and China, together with translations of the
                    regulations for carrying out the above ordinances.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peter Augustus
                    Jay.</hi></signed></closer>









